course: dictionary
lesson: 1428
title: Carnivore: the meat eater
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A carnivore is an animal that eats mainly meat, other animals. You can work out the meaning from the words around it. «Herbivores eat plants, carnivores eat animals, and omnivores eat both.» Plant-eater and animal-eater sit side by side, so carnivore must be the meat-eater.
explain: «A lion, a shark, an eagle and a wolf are all carnivores.» Each of these hunts and catches other animals to live. «In a food chain such as grass, rabbit, fox, the fox is a carnivore.» The arrows point from the food to the eater, so the arrow from rabbit to fox shows the fox eats the rabbit.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Real cats are carnivores: they need meat.» If you put "animals that eat mainly meat" in place of carnivores, the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
fact: A carnivore is an animal that eats mainly meat, other animals.
fact: Herbivores eat plants, carnivores eat animals, and omnivores eat both.
fact: Carnivores often have sharp teeth and claws for catching and tearing meat.
fact: An animal that hunts other animals is a predator, and the animal it hunts is its prey.
fact: A carnivorous plant, like the Venus flytrap, traps and eats insects.
exercise: «A cat is a carnivore.» What does carnivore mean? | *An animal that eats mainly meat | An animal that eats plants only | A plant that traps insects | An animal with no teeth
exercise: «Herbivores eat plants, carnivores eat animals, and omnivores eat both.» Which word means an animal that eats both plants and animals? | *Omnivore | Herbivore | Carnivore | Predator
exercise: Which animal is a carnivore? | Horse | Rabbit | Sheep | *Eagle
test: In a food chain such as grass, rabbit, fox, what is the fox? | Herbivore | Omnivore | Producer | *Carnivore
test: Which plant is carnivorous? | Oak tree | *Venus flytrap | Daisy | Sunflower
exam: «Real cats are carnivores: they need meat.» Using the words around it, what does carnivore mean? | *An animal that eats mainly meat | A plant that drinks water | An animal that only eats grass | Any animal that lives on a farm
